§ 37.01 ELECTION OF COUNTY ASSESSMENT.
   Pursuant to the authority of KRS 132.285, the City Council elects to adopt
and use the annual Kenton County assessment for property situated within its
corporate limits as a basis for its ad valorem property tax.
(Ord. 1-8-86, passed 8-26-86)
§ 37.02 TAX RATE ESTABLISHED.
   The tax rate for each year on all real, mixed, and personal property
situated within the corporate limits of the city and not exempt by law shall be
as established by ordinance of City Council.
(Ord. 1-8-86, passed 8-26-86)
Cross reference:
   Ad valorem taxation rates, see
Table of Special Ordinances, Table X.
§ 37.03 DISPOSITION OF FUNDS.
   All revenues derived and collected from this tax may be disbursed for one or
more of the following purposes: police protection, public works, General Fund,
contingencies, or miscellaneous.
(Ord. 1-8-86, passed 8-26-86)
§ 37.04 DUE DATE; PENALTIES.
   (A)   Taxes shall be collected in the city by the City Clerk. All taxes
shall be due and payable by December 31 in the year of the assessment. Any
taxpayer who pays his city taxes in full by the end of the business day on
November 1 in the year of the assessment shall be entitled to a two percent
(2%) discount on the amount of the ad valorem tax. The discount shall not apply
to the garbage assessment.
   (B)   Ad valorem taxes become delinquent on January 1 of the year following
the year of the assessment. After a tax bill becomes delinquent, a fifteen
percent (15%) penalty shall be added thereon, together with interest which
shall accrue on all unpaid taxes at the rate of six percent (6%) per annum will
be attached effective January 1 until paid, plus the cost of collection,
including without limitation, court costs and attorney’s fees, with a minimum
interest charge of ten dollars ($10.00).
(Ord. 1-8-86, passed 8-26-86; Am. Ord. 1999-0-08, passed 9-13-99; Am. Ord.
2000-0-15, passed 9-11-00; Am. Ord. 2017-O-11, passed 9-11-17; Am. Ord. 2018-O-
11, passed 9-10-18; Am. Ord. 2019- O-05, passed 9-16-19)
§ 37.05 COMPENSATION FOR CITY ATTORNEY FOR REPRESENTATION IN ACTIONS IN WHICH
ENFORCEMENT OF LIEN IS INVOLVED.
   For each civil action filed by the City Attorney for the city for the
collection of delinquent taxes, penalties, interest, fees, commissions,
charges, or other expenses incurred by reason of delinquency in the payment of
taxes or in the process of collecting it, a reasonable attorney fee shall be
paid by the delinquent taxpayers and recovered as part of the cost of
prosecution of the civil action by the city.
(Ord. 3-5-79, passed 5-24-79; Am. Ord. 2004-O-08, passed 5-3-04)
§ 37.06 LIEN.
   In order to secure the payment of the ad valorem taxes hereby levied and
assessed, and all penalties, interest, fees, commissions, charges and other
expenses, including court costs and attorneys fees, incurred by reason of any
delinquency in the payment thereof or the process of collection, the city shall
have a lien upon the property upon which such taxes are hereby levied and
assessed. The lien shall have priority over all other obligations or
liabilities for which the property is liable, except state and county taxes,
with which it has equal priority.
(Ord. 1999-0-08, passed 9-13-99)
